[17592186493316 1072 #uuid "7e3f1a4a-bfde-54af-80e2-4cc4e890e6fc" 13194139535309 17592186045443 true] [17592186493316 1074 "Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f'(x)=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(10 x^{2} + 5 x)=20 x + 5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the slope of the tangent line is\n\n$$\nm=f'(1)=25=25,\n$$\n\nand therefore the slope of the normal line is\n\n$$\nm'=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{(25)}=- \\frac{1}{25}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(15)&=- \\frac{1}{25}(x-(1))\\\\y&=- \\frac{1}{25}x-(- \\frac{1}{25})+(15)\\\\y&=- \\frac{1}{25}x+\\frac{376}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we find the point of intersection with the $x$-axis by setting $y=0$ and solving the resulting equation. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}- \\frac{1}{25}x+\\frac{376}{25}&=0\\\\x&=376.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the normal line intersects the $x$-axis at $(376,0).$" 13194139535309 17592186045443 true] [17592186493317 1080 "-1080" 13194139535309 17592186045443 true] [17592186493317 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535309 17592186045443 true] [17592186493317 1083 #uuid "93fb4c05-1e1a-5463-aeeb-5bdc06ba8f62" 13194139535309 17592186045443 true] [17592186493318 1068 #edb/ref 17592186493309 13194139535309 17592186045443 true] [17592186493318 1068 #edb/ref 17592186493319 13194139535309 17592186045443 true] [17592186493318 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535309 17592186045443 true] [17592186493318 1071 "Find where the normal line to the curve $y=\\frac{20}{x}+10$ at the point $(1,30)$ intersects the $x$-axis.\n\nThe normal line intersects the $x$-axis at\n$($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}} $).$" 13194139535309 17592186045443 true] [17592186493318 1072 #uuid "9c1268dd-9a0b-5590-983e-596506fe3286" 13194139535309 17592186045443 true] [17592186493318 1074 "Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f'(x)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(\\frac{20}{x}+10)\\\\&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(10 + \\frac{20}{x})\\\\&=-20x^{-2}\\\\&=- \\frac{20}{x^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the slope of the tangent line is\n\n$$\nm=f'(1)=-20=-20,\n$$\n\nand therefore the slope of the normal line is\n\n$$\nm'=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{(-20)}=\\frac{1}{20}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(30)&=\\frac{1}{20}(x-(1))\\\\y&=\\frac{1}{20}x-(\\frac{1}{20})+(30)\\\\y&=\\frac{1}{20}x+\\frac{599}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we find the point of intersection with the $x$-axis by setting $y=0$ and solving the resulting equation. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{20}x+\\frac{599}{20}&=0\\\\x&=-599.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the normal line intersects the  $x$-axis at $(-599,0).$" 13194139535309 17592186045443 true] [17592186493319 1075 #edb/ref 17592186493320 13194139535309 17592186045443 true] [17592186493319 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139535309 17592186045443 true] [17592186493319 1077 "field-2" 13194139535309 17592186045443 true] [17592186493319 1078 #edb/ref 17592186493320 13194139535309 17592186045443 true] [17592186493319 1079 #uuid "a11eaf98-7e1d-530f-93f1-50c6c3aa85a7" 13194139535309 17592186045443 true] [17592186493320 1080 "0" 13194139535309 17592186045443 true] [17592186493320 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535309 17592186045443 true] [17592186493320 1083 #uuid "ba9c2120-ea78-56ae-b7da-fc8f913f4ff6" 13194139535309 17592186045443 true] [17592186493321 1068 #edb/ref 17592186493315 13194139535309 17592186045443 true] [17592186493321 1068 #edb/ref 17592186493323 13194139535309 17592186045443 true] [17592186493321 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535309 17592186045443 true] [17592186493321 1071 "Find where the normal line to the curve $y=18 x^{2} - 36 x + 30$ at the point $(0,30)$ intersects the $x$-axis.\n\nThe normal line intersects the $x$-axis at\n$($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}} $).$" 13194139535309 17592186045443 true] [17592186493321 1072 #uuid "c3c9763c-f1e1-51a2-887f-38a4a610161d" 13194139535309 17592186045443 true] [17592186493321 1074 "Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\nf'(x)=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(18 x^{2} - 36 x + 30)=36 x - 36.\n$$\n\nSo the slope of the tangent line is\n\n$$\nm=f'(0)=-36=-36,\n$$\n\nand therefore the slope of the normal line is\n\n$$\nm'=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{(-36)}=\\frac{1}{36}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(30)&=\\frac{1}{36}(x-(0))\\\\y&=\\frac{1}{36}x+30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we find the point of intersection with the $x$-axis by setting $y=0$ and solving the resulting equation. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{36}x+30&=0\\\\\\frac{1}{36}x&=-30\\\\x&=-1080.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the normal line intersects the $x$-axis at $(-1080,0).$" 13194139535309 17592186045443 true] [17592186493322 1080 "(25,0)" 13194139535309 17592186045443 true] [17592186493322 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535309 17592186045443 true] [17592186493322 1083 #uuid "cb3d8d25-8bfa-5e2a-b032-69c3782c0eb7" 13194139535309 17592186045443 true] [17592186493323 1075 #edb/ref 17592186493308 13194139535309 17592186045443 true] [17592186493323 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139535309 17592186045443 true] [17592186493323 1077 "field-2" 13194139535309 17592186045443 true] [17592186493323 1078 #edb/ref 17592186493308 13194139535309 17592186045443 true] [17592186493323 1079 #uuid "f7f48b25-30b8-5af5-8b60-15f91577b14d" 13194139535309 17592186045443 true] [17592186493324 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186092385.py" 13194139535309 17592186045443 true] [17592186493324 1169 #uuid "6f93f05c-93ce-5432-b4e0-7ec958ee8e90" 13194139535309 17592186045443 true]] :edb/tempids {"028288df-333f-57f2-9e25-7548b283399c" 17592186493307 "17fbaf02-25c3-5f36-8455-1d21e7ade415" 17592186493308 "24d2eda6-5f52-58d1-8821-c19db30c5bf9" 17592186493309 "30a55d4b-f895-53a5-a364-ce5fddbb6ae1" 17592186493310 "4079920d-ee6c-5086-9aa8-97eb49b915c2" 17592186493311 "40ab1d54-64ea-58e4-9d91-d527f34b3bee" 17592186493312 "59d2a5db-49a2-